>> title: Grilled Cheese
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: cheese, bread, griddle, sandwich, lunch
>> counters: Diner, Deli
>> aka: grilled cheese, grilled cheese sandwich, toasted cheese, cheese toastie, toastie
>> pairs-with: tomato-soup
>> servings: 2
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: butter the outside faces, edge to edge
>> step.2: two cheeses, one melts and one tastes
>> step.3: griddle low, 4 min, flip, 3 min

Spread @salted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g; soft, not melted) over one face of each of @white sandwich bread{4%slices}, right to the crust. Soft butter spread thin browns evenly; melted butter poured in the pan burns in the middle and leaves the corners pale. Mayonnaise on the outside browns faster and tastes of mayonnaise — the diner uses butter.

Fill @&(~1)buttered bread{} with @American cheese{4%slices} and @sharp cheddar{2%oz}(60 g; grated), butter facing out. Two cheeses because one job is melting and the other is tasting of something: American alone is bland, cheddar alone breaks and goes oily.

Griddle @&(~1)built sandwiches{} in a #skillet{} over medium-low heat ~fry{4%min}, flip once and press with a spatula, then ~fry{3%min}. Low heat is the whole method — anything hotter browns the bread before the middle has melted.
